Hi Karl, hi all,

I hope all of you are safe :)

Currently, I'm trying to run the function scan1snps() with a genoprob that I converted from probs with a DOQTL format (I used the function probs_doqtl_to_qtl2() package qtl2convert)

I am able to make QTL plots and effect plots but, when I try to run scan1snps() I have an error:

"Error in scan1snps(genoprobs = pr_f_doqtl, map = map_3, pheno = dato,  :   genoprobs and map have different numbers of markers".

I know that the error probably came from the use of probs_doqtl_to_qtl2() function, but I don't understand why, if I originated genoprobs and map from the same source.

The files to reproduce the error can be found at https://drive.google.com/file/d/100Dp7lFIR6MjWZP-y3sL52cjqh470bLO/view?usp=sharing (I couldn't attach without exceeding the permitted size)

